#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:331
msgid "Questions and answers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:169
msgid "Go to Opening Hours → Add set, give it a name (e.g. “Shop”) and enter your weekly hours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:170
msgid "Check the Holidays tab: choose your federal state and decide for each holiday whether you are closed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:171
msgid "Save. Then edit the page where the hours should appear and add the block “Opening Hours” (or paste the shortcode shown next to the set)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:172
msgid "Add the block “Opening Hours Notice” to the start page or the header area once; it stays invisible until a planned change is due."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:173
msgid "Before a holiday or vacation, add a period in the Periods tab. The notice appears automatically ahead of time and disappears afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:179
msgid "A set is one complete collection of opening hours. Most sites need just one. Create several sets if you have different hours for different things, for example “Practice” and “Phone hours”, or two locations. Blocks and shortcodes always refer to one set; the <strong>default set</strong> (see Settings) is used when nothing is specified."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:180
msgid "The set name is what visitors may see as a heading. The <strong>slug</strong> shown in the list and in the sidebar box is the technical name used in shortcodes; it is derived from the name when the set is first saved and does not change afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:185
msgid "The weekly hours that apply whenever no period and no holiday says otherwise. Each weekday has one of three modes:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:188
#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:220
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:1
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:3
msgid "Closed"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:188
msgid "The day is shown as closed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:189
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:1
msgid "Open"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:189
msgid "Enter one or more <strong>time slots</strong>, e.g. 08:00–12:00 and 14:00–18:00 for a lunch break. Times use the 24-hour format HH:MM. An end time earlier than the start time (e.g. 18:00–02:00) means the slot runs into the next day; use 24:00 for “until midnight”."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:190
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:1
msgid "Text"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:190
msgid "Shows a text instead of times, e.g. “by appointment” or “on request”."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:191
#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:206
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:1
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:2
msgid "Note"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:191
msgid "Optional remark shown next to the hours of that day, e.g. “Emergency service only”. Notes can be hidden in the display options."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:192
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:1
msgid "Copy to Tue–Fri"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:192
msgid "Copies Monday’s entry to Tuesday through Friday to save typing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:199
msgid "Periods are date ranges with different hours: vacation, company holidays, reduced summer hours, extended hours before Christmas, a training day. They are planned in advance and take effect on their own. Past periods are hidden in the editor but kept."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:202
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:1
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:202
msgid "Shown in the notice and used as the row label in the editor, e.g. “Summer break”."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:203
msgid "From / Until (inclusive)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:203
msgid "First and last day of the period. A single day has the same start and end date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:204
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:1
msgid "During this period"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:204
msgid "<strong>Closed</strong> – closed on every day of the range. <strong>Same hours every day</strong> – one set of time slots that applies to every day, e.g. 10:00–14:00 between the years. <strong>Different weekly hours</strong> – a complete alternative week, e.g. summer hours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:205
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:1
msgid "Lead time for the notice (days)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:205
msgid "How many days before the start the notice block starts announcing this period. Empty uses the value from the settings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:206
msgid "Optional text shown with the hours and available as {note} in the notice, e.g. an emergency phone number."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:207
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:2
msgid "Repeats every year (same dates)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:207
msgid "For fixed yearly closures such as 24 December – 2 January. The year of the dates does not matter; ranges may span the turn of the year."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:208
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:2
msgid "Also open on public holidays in this period"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:208
msgid "Normally a public holiday inside a period with alternative hours still follows the holiday rule (usually closed). Tick this if the period’s hours should apply on holidays too, e.g. a Christmas market stall."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:211
msgid "<strong>Which hours win?</strong> On any given day the plugin checks in this order: 1. a period marked “closed”, 2. a public holiday (unless its rule is “regular hours” or the period ignores holidays), 3. a period with alternative hours (the shorter, more specific one first), 4. the regular weekly hours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:216
msgid "German public holidays are calculated automatically for the chosen <strong>federal state</strong>, including moveable feasts such as Easter and Whitsun, and the Day of Repentance in Saxony. Some holidays apply only in parts of a state (e.g. Corpus Christi in Catholic communities of Saxony and Thuringia, Assumption Day and the Augsburg Peace Festival in Bavaria); tick them under <strong>regional holidays</strong> if they apply to you."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:217
msgid "For each holiday choose a rule:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:220
msgid "The default. The day is shown as closed with the holiday’s name as a note."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:221
msgid "The holiday is ignored; the normal weekday hours apply (e.g. restaurants, petrol stations)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:222
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:3
msgid "Special hours"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:222
msgid "Enter the time slots that apply on this holiday, e.g. a bakery open 07:00–10:00 on Easter Sunday."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:225
msgid "The table shows the dates for the current and the next year so you can check them. Holidays are included in the “current week” view, in the notice-free status and in the structured data; they do not create notices."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:230
msgid "Defaults for how this set is shown. Every block and shortcode can override each option individually."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:233
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:3
#: build/blocks/opening-hours/index.js:1
msgid "Layout"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:233
msgid "<strong>Table</strong> – one row per day (group), best for sidebars and contact pages. <strong>List</strong> – definition list with the same content, useful when tables look heavy in your theme. <strong>Compact</strong> – everything in a single line, e.g. “Mon–Fri 9–18 h · Sat 9–12 h”, for footers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:234
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:3
#: build/blocks/opening-hours/index.js:1
msgid "Time format"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:234
msgid "24-hour (09:00–18:00), short 24-hour (9–18 h, minutes only when needed) or 12-hour (9:00 am–6:00 pm)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:235
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:3
msgid "Week shown"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:235
msgid "<strong>Current week</strong> shows Monday to Sunday of this week with holidays and periods already applied, so a visitor sees what really applies. <strong>Regular hours only</strong> always shows the plain weekly schedule; combine it with the notice block to announce deviations."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:236
msgid "Group days with equal hours"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:236
msgid "Merges consecutive days with identical hours into one row, e.g. “Mon–Fri”. Days that differ (a holiday, a note) start a new row."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:237
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:3
#: build/blocks/opening-hours/index.js:1
msgid "Highlight today"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:237
msgid "Marks today’s row so it can be styled (bold background by default)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:238
#: build/admin/set-editor.js:3
#: build/blocks/opening-hours/index.js:1
msgid "Show notes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:238
msgid "Shows the notes of days, periods and holiday names below the hours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:245
msgid "Optionally the plugin adds machine-readable opening hours (schema.org “openingHoursSpecification”, including upcoming exceptions) to the page so search engines can show them. Enter the business type, name and website URL. Leave this <strong>off</strong> if an SEO plugin (e.g. Yoast Local SEO, Rank Math) already describes your business, otherwise search engines may see two different businesses."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:250
msgid "In the block editor search for “Opening Hours”. All three blocks pick the set in the sidebar and support colors, typography and spacing from your theme."
msgstr ""

