msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:334
msgid "The website still shows old hours after I saved."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:334
msgid "Your site probably uses a caching plugin. The plugin asks the common caches to refresh when you save, but some need a manual “purge cache”. The “open now” status and notices switch correctly even on cached pages."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:335
msgid "I want to announce a change without changing the hours yet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:335
msgid "Create a period with a start date in the future. The notice block announces it from the lead time onwards while the regular hours keep applying until the start date."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:336
msgid "We are open on a holiday this year only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:336
msgid "Add a period for that single day with “same hours every day” and tick “also open on public holidays in this period”."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:337
msgid "We close early on one specific day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:337
msgid "Add a single-day period with “same hours every day” and the reduced time slot. Add a short lead time so visitors are warned."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:338
msgid "How do I style the output?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/HelpPage.php:338
msgid "Use the block’s color and typography settings, or add CSS in your theme: the table uses the class <code>rmd-oh</code>, notices <code>rmd-oh-notice</code>, the status <code>rmd-oh-status</code>. Colors and spacing are exposed as CSS custom properties, see the README on GitHub."
